# Atlas — scenarios through the public API. Works with the VS Code REST Client extension and Visual Studio.
# Start everything first: ./scripts/run.ps1 (or ./scripts/run.sh). See README "Driving the provider stand-ins".
#
# All personal data below is synthetic. Images are base64 text; the provider stub looks for markers inside them:
#   c3ludGhldGljLXBhc3Nwb3J0                              "synthetic-passport"                (happy path)
#   c3ludGhldGljLXBhc3Nwb3J0IGlkbm93OklOVkFMSUQ=          "... idnow:INVALID"
#   c3ludGhldGljLXBhc3Nwb3J0IGlkbm93OkZBQ0VfTUlTTUFUQ0g=  "... idnow:FACE_MISMATCH"
#   c3ludGhldGljLXBhc3Nwb3J0IGlkbm93OklOQ09OQ0xVU0lWRQ==  "... idnow:INCONCLUSIVE"
#   c3ludGhldGljLXBhc3Nwb3J0IGlkbm93OkZMQUtZ              "... idnow:FLAKY"   (503 twice, then OK)
#   c3ludGhldGljLXBhc3Nwb3J0IGlkbm93OkRPV04=              "... idnow:DOWN"    (503 until you "recover" it, see stubs.http)
# World-Check rules match the last name: PossibleMatch*, AutoClear*, Sanctioned*, Flaky*, Unreachable*.

@onboarding = http://127.0.0.1:5100
@customer = Bearer dev:customer:device-1
@staff = Bearer dev:staff:teller-12
@selfie = c3ludGhldGljLXNlbGZpZQ==

### 1. Happy path (MB): 202 IN_PROGRESS, then APPROVED within seconds
# @name happy
POST {{onboarding}}/applications
Authorization: {{customer}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Ana", "lastName": "Example", "dateOfBirth": "1991-03-04",
  "country": "MB", "nationalId": "0403991450016",
  "email": "ana@example.test", "phone": "+000 000 000",
  "documents": [
    { "type": "PASSPORT", "image": "c3ludGhldGljLXBhc3Nwb3J0" },
    { "type": "SELFIE", "image": "{{selfie}}" }
  ],
  "termsAccepted": true
}

### 1b. Status of the application above (repeat until APPROVED)
GET {{onboarding}}/applications/{{happy.response.body.$.applicationId}}
Authorization: {{customer}}

### 2. Possible sanctions match: UNDER_REVIEW until an officer resolves the case (stubs.http → resolve)
# @name possibleMatch
POST {{onboarding}}/applications
Authorization: {{customer}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Test", "lastName": "PossibleMatch", "dateOfBirth": "1980-01-01",
  "country": "MA", "nationalId": "0101980450016",
  "email": "pm@example.test", "phone": "+000 000 000",
  "documents": [
    { "type": "PASSPORT", "image": "c3ludGhldGljLXBhc3Nwb3J0" },
    { "type": "SELFIE", "image": "{{selfie}}" }
  ],
  "termsAccepted": true
}

### 2b. Status (UNDER_REVIEW, and stays so: nothing is decided automatically)
GET {{onboarding}}/applications/{{possibleMatch.response.body.$.applicationId}}
Authorization: {{customer}}

### 3. Confirmed match, resolved by the stub's simulated officer after 20s: UNDER_REVIEW, then REJECTED / NOT_ELIGIBLE
# @name sanctioned
POST {{onboarding}}/applications
Authorization: {{customer}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Test", "lastName": "Sanctioned", "dateOfBirth": "1975-05-05",
  "country": "ME", "nationalId": "1234567890",
  "email": "s@example.test", "phone": "+000 000 000",
  "documents": [
    { "type": "PASSPORT", "image": "c3ludGhldGljLXBhc3Nwb3J0" },
    { "type": "SELFIE", "image": "{{selfie}}" }
  ],
  "termsAccepted": true
}

### 3b. Status
GET {{onboarding}}/applications/{{sanctioned.response.body.$.applicationId}}
Authorization: {{customer}}

### 4. MD: in-person activation required. AWAITING_BRANCH_VISIT, then staff activate, then APPROVED
# @name branch
POST {{onboarding}}/applications
Authorization: {{customer}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Test", "lastName": "Branch", "dateOfBirth": "1988-08-08",
  "country": "MD", "nationalId": "1234567890",
  "email": "b@example.test", "phone": "+000 000 000",
  "documents": [
    { "type": "ID_CARD", "image": "c3ludGhldGljLXBhc3Nwb3J0" },
    { "type": "SELFIE", "image": "{{selfie}}" }
  ],
  "termsAccepted": true
}

### 4b. Status (AWAITING_BRANCH_VISIT)
GET {{onboarding}}/applications/{{branch.response.body.$.applicationId}}
Authorization: {{customer}}

### 4c. Branch staff check the person in front of them (audited read)
GET {{onboarding}}/branch/applications/{{branch.response.body.$.applicationId}}/applicant
Authorization: {{staff}}

### 4d. Branch staff record the wet signature: account opening starts
POST {{onboarding}}/branch/applications/{{branch.response.body.$.applicationId}}/activation
Authorization: {{staff}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "branchCode": "MD-001", "signedFormReference": "form-2026-0001" }

### 5. MF resident without a Personal Number: passport number in lieu (nationality required)
POST {{onboarding}}/applications
Authorization: {{customer}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Test", "lastName": "Resident", "dateOfBirth": "1995-02-02",
  "country": "MF", "passportNumber": "AB1234567", "nationality": "SY",
  "email": "r@example.test", "phone": "+000 000 000",
  "documents": [
    { "type": "PASSPORT", "image": "c3ludGhldGljLXBhc3Nwb3J0" },
    { "type": "SELFIE", "image": "{{selfie}}" }
  ],
  "termsAccepted": true
}

### 6. IDNow down: stays IN_PROGRESS and retries with backoff (watch Seq); never rejected. Recover it in stubs.http.
# @name outage
POST {{onboarding}}/applications
Authorization: {{customer}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Test", "lastName": "Outage", "dateOfBirth": "1990-01-01",
  "country": "MC", "nationalId": "12345678A",
  "email": "o@example.test", "phone": "+000 000 000",
  "documents": [
    { "type": "PASSPORT", "image": "c3ludGhldGljLXBhc3Nwb3J0IGlkbm93OkRPV04=" },
    { "type": "SELFIE", "image": "{{selfie}}" }
  ],
  "termsAccepted": true
}

### 6b. Status
GET {{onboarding}}/applications/{{outage.response.body.$.applicationId}}
Authorization: {{customer}}

### 7. Forged document: REJECTED / IDENTITY_NOT_VERIFIED
POST {{onboarding}}/applications
Authorization: {{customer}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Test", "lastName": "Forged", "dateOfBirth": "1990-01-01",
  "country": "MB", "nationalId": "0101990450016",
  "email": "f@example.test", "phone": "+000 000 000",
  "documents": [
    { "type": "PASSPORT", "image": "c3ludGhldGljLXBhc3Nwb3J0IGlkbm93OklOVkFMSUQ=" },
    { "type": "SELFIE", "image": "{{selfie}}" }
  ],
  "termsAccepted": true
}

### 8. Validation: MD identifier in an MB application → 400 with errors.nationalId
POST {{onboarding}}/applications
Authorization: {{customer}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Test", "lastName": "Invalid", "dateOfBirth": "1990-01-01",
  "country": "MB", "nationalId": "1234567890",
  "email": "i@example.test", "phone": "+000 000 000",
  "documents": [
    { "type": "PASSPORT", "image": "c3ludGhldGljLXBhc3Nwb3J0" },
    { "type": "SELFIE", "image": "{{selfie}}" }
  ],
  "termsAccepted": true
}

### 9. Idempotency: send this twice. Same key, same answer, one application.
POST {{onboarding}}/applications
Authorization: {{customer}}
Idempotency-Key: fixed-key-for-replay-demo
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Test", "lastName": "Tunnel", "dateOfBirth": "1990-01-01",
  "country": "MB", "nationalId": "0101990450016",
  "email": "t@example.test", "phone": "+000 000 000",
  "documents": [
    { "type": "PASSPORT", "image": "c3ludGhldGljLXBhc3Nwb3J0" },
    { "type": "SELFIE", "image": "{{selfie}}" }
  ],
  "termsAccepted": true
}
